# Orbit UI rules

## Product feel
- Premium consumer app for students, never an admin dashboard.
- Mobile first: design at 390px, max content width ~430px, then scale up.
- One primary action per card.

## Canvas and surfaces
- Canvas: `bg-orbit-bg` (#0A1020). Never pure black or light gray for student shells.
- Cards: `orbit-card` / `rounded-card` (20px) + `border-white/[0.08]`. Never flat grey borders (`border-gray-700`).
- Raised blocks: `bg-orbit-surface-raised` (#131F3B).

## Section headers
- Use `.orbit-eyebrow` (11px bold uppercase tracking-eyebrow text-slate-400).
- Pair with electric blue `.orbit-link` ("View all →") on the right when there is a list.

## Subjects and categories
- Math → `.card-math`, Science → `.card-science`, Chemistry → `.card-chem`, English → `.card-english`.
- Grow explore: `.card-category-interests|clubs|competitions|skills`.

## Buttons and type
- Primary CTA: `.orbit-btn-primary` (#1E7BFF + `shadow-glow-primary`).
- Fonts: Plus Jakarta Sans headings (`font-heading`), Inter body (`font-sans`).
- Tokens live in `design-tokens.json` and `src/styles/orbit-design.css`. Prefer semantic classes over raw hex in new code.

## Nav
- Bottom nav active tab: electric blue icon + soft glow, not a heavy filled pill.
- Top bar: ORBIT mark + bell (badge) + theme + logout on root tabs.

## Motion
- Prefer one entrance per screen; press scale ~0.98 on primary buttons.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.

## Copy
- Sentence case. Verbs first on buttons. Deadlines as "Due tomorrow", not alarm words.
